  "assets": [
    {
      "uuid": "2fed3504-9f6a-4270-8fed-35049f6a5270",
      "name": "Getting Started.md",
      "path": "Assets/Tutorials/Getting Started.md",
      "assetType": "other",
      "mimeType": "text/markdown",
      "byteLength": 665,
      "source": "---\ndismissible: true\ntemplate: coin-trail\n---\n# Coin Trail\n\nCollect six checkpoints in order. A gentle keyboard game with scoring, completion, and restart.\n\nWASD / arrow keys move. Collect the green checkpoint; the next appears after collection. Avoid pink circles. R restarts, including after a win or loss.\n\n## Edit and verify\n\nSelect named objects in Scene and change one component at a time. Play checks runtime behavior; Stop restores authored values. Save, reopen, and use Manage → Build to verify persistence and export. These are small complete checkpoint games; edit CheckpointGame.rhai to change course rules. All movement and hit tests use world units.\n",
      "sourceModified": 0,
      "importedAt": 0,
      "width": 0,
      "height": 0,
      "duration": 0,
      "fontFamily": "",
      "settings": {
        "filterMode": "Linear",
        "compression": "Lossless",
        "pixelsPerUnit": 100,
        "spriteRegion": null,
        "pivot": {
          "x": 0.5,
          "y": 0.5
        },
        "atlas": false
      },
      "pipeline": {
        "importerVersion": "template-4.2",
        "platform": "web",
        "sourceHash": "3fb36a83db77ca9a1ff72e1c8803f4ab9f646b6af7099ed2074732b6300d50b4",
        "artifactHash": "3fb36a83db77ca9a1ff72e1c8803f4ab9f646b6af7099ed2074732b6300d50b4",
        "contentHash": "3fb36a83db77ca9a1ff72e1c8803f4ab9f646b6af7099ed2074732b6300d50b4",
        "cacheKey": "3fb36a83db77ca9a1ff72e1c8803f4ab9f646b6af7099ed2074732b6300d50b4",
        "status": "ready",
        "lastValidSource": "---\ndismissible: true\ntemplate: coin-trail\n---\n# Coin Trail\n\nCollect six checkpoints in order. A gentle keyboard game with scoring, completion, and restart.\n\nWASD / arrow keys move. Collect the green checkpoint; the next appears after collection. Avoid pink circles. R restarts, including after a win or loss.\n\n## Edit and verify\n\nSelect named objects in Scene and change one component at a time. Play checks runtime behavior; Stop restores authored values. Save, reopen, and use Manage → Build to verify persistence and export. These are small complete checkpoint games; edit CheckpointGame.rhai to change course rules. All movement and hit tests use world units.\n",
        "error": "",
        "dependencies": [],
        "reverseDependencies": [],
        "cacheHit": false
      }
